Third-party notice (read this before you redistribute a compiled build)

This repository's own source code is MIT, as above. It does not compile or run
on its own, however: it references two NuGet packages published by the
BetterLyrics project, and the built .blp is loaded by the BetterLyrics host.

  * BetterLyrics.Sdk 1.0.3       - GPL-3.0-or-later
    https://github.com/jayfunc/BetterLyrics/tree/dev/src/BetterLyrics.Sdk
  * BetterLyrics.DevTools 1.0.3  - MIT
    https://github.com/BetterLyrics/BetterLyrics.DevTools
  * BetterLyrics host 1.3.544.0  - GPL-3.0
    https://github.com/BetterLyrics/BetterLyrics

BetterLyrics.Sdk is GPL-3.0-or-later. A compiled plugin links against it, so the
binary as a whole is a work that must be distributed under the terms of the
GPL-3.0, even though the sources in this repository are offered under the MIT
license. The release artefacts attached to GitHub Releases are published on
that basis. If that distinction matters to you, treat the built .blp as
GPL-3.0 and this source tree as MIT.

